<main class="site-page info-page help-page">
    <header class="page-intro">
        <p class="page-eyebrow">Player guide</p>
        <h1>Set up a session that works for you.</h1>
        <p>Adjust the eye colors, tile mix, board, and speed before or during a game.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="help-layout">
        <nav class="help-toc" aria-label="On this page">
            <p>On this page</p>
            <a href="#color-setup">Color setup</a>
            <a href="#tile-mix">Tile mix</a>
            <a href="#game-settings">Board and speed</a>
            <a href="#run-stats">Run stats</a>
            <a href="#controls">Controls</a>
            <a href="#saved-settings">Saved settings</a>
        </nav>

        <div class="help-sections">
            <section class="doc-section" id="color-setup">
                <p class="section-index">Color setup</p>
                <h2>Set the colors for each eye</h2>
                <p>With anaglyph glasses on, tune each eye color until its test block disappears through the opposite lens but stays visible through the intended lens. The black preview matches the game background.</p>
                <ol>
                    <li>Open the game and choose <strong>Settings</strong>, then <strong>Left eye color</strong>.</li>
                    <li>Look through your right lens and adjust the color until the test block blends into the black background. Check that it remains visible through your left lens.</li>
                    <li>Repeat for <strong>Right eye color</strong>, using your left lens to hide the block and your right lens to see it.</li>
                </ol>
                <p>Color perception and glasses vary, so adjust the colors in your own setup.</p>
            </section>

            <section class="doc-section" id="tile-mix">
                <p class="section-index">Tile mix</p>
                <h2>Choose how colors are assigned</h2>
                <p><strong>Color by shapes</strong> gives each new shape one eye color. <strong>Color by cells</strong> assigns a color to each cell independently.</p>
                <p>In <strong>Red / blue tile mix</strong>, adjust the chance for each channel in 5% steps. The red and blue shares always add up to 100%.</p>
            </section>

            <section class="doc-section" id="game-settings">
                <p class="section-index">Playfield</p>
                <h2>Adjust the board and speed</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Board size</strong> changes rows and columns. The board resizes to fit the available screen.</li>
                    <li><strong>Speed level</strong> changes how quickly pieces fall. You can lock the level to keep the pace steady.</li>
                    <li>Settings can be changed between games or from the in-game toolbar.</li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section class="doc-section" id="run-stats">
                <p class="section-index">During a run</p>
                <h2>Read your stats</h2>
                <dl class="guide-definitions">
                    <div><dt>Score</dt><dd>Points earned. Clearing several rows at once earns more points.</dd></div>
                    <div><dt>Lines cleared</dt><dd>The total number of full rows removed from the board.</dd></div>
                    <div><dt>Level</dt><dd>The current fall speed setting.</dd></div>
                    <div><dt>Next piece</dt><dd>A preview of the piece that will enter play after the current one lands.</dd></div>
                </dl>
            </section>

            <section class="doc-section" id="controls">
                <p class="section-index">Controls</p>
                <h2>Move and manage pieces</h2>
                <dl class="guide-definitions guide-controls">
                    <div><dt>Left / right</dt><dd>Move one cell.</dd></div>
                    <div><dt>Down</dt><dd>Move down one cell.</dd></div>
                    <div><dt>Up</dt><dd>Rotate the piece.</dd></div>
                    <div><dt>Space</dt><dd>Drop the piece.</dd></div>
                    <div><dt>P</dt><dd>Pause or resume.</dd></div>
                    <div><dt>Q / Escape</dt><dd>Start a new game.</dd></div>
                    <div><dt>G</dt><dd>Show or hide the grid.</dd></div>
                </dl>
            </section>

            <section class="doc-section" id="saved-settings">
                <p class="section-index">Your browser</p>
                <h2>Settings are saved automatically</h2>
                <p>Colors, tile mix, board size, and speed settings stay in this browser between visits. Use <strong>Save settings</strong> and <strong>Load settings</strong> in the Settings menu to manage a saved copy manually.</p>
            </section>
        </div>
    </div>
</main>
